headscale on FenrirOS
=====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no configuration, no
user, no pre-auth key and no node.

1. cp /usr/share/doc/headscale/config-example.yaml /etc/headscale/config.yaml
   and edit it (server_url, listen_addr, prefixes, DNS). The sample listens on
   127.0.0.1:8080 and keeps its state (SQLite, noise key) in /var/lib/headscale.
2. dinitctl enable headscale
3. Administer it with the CLI over the unix socket /run/headscale/headscale.sock
   (group headscale; add your admin user to it): headscale users create ...,
   headscale preauthkeys create ..., headscale nodes list.

TLS and a reverse proxy are the administrator's choice; update checks are
controlled by disable_check_updates in the configuration.
